Found during k85 (worker). parseSources (src/config.ts) takes `git`/`ref` only when typeof string, so `ref: 123` silently drops the pin (installs HEAD) instead of a ConfigError. `ref: ""` fetches HEAD but check finds no matching ref and reports changed every session. Fix: a present non-string git/ref (or local/url) is a ConfigError naming file, source and key; an empty ref is either refused or treated as absent consistently in resolve and check. Also: skills/skilletor/SKILL.md (~line 97, the `ref` field) could say a ref must be a plain git ref name (k85: no leading "-", no whitespace/control chars/~^:?*[\\/../@{) – one clause.

2026-09-26 16:22 From k83 (worker): GitSource.cacheDir treats ref "" as unpinned (URL-only cache) but resolve fetches the empty ref, so an unpinned name and a ref:"" name on the same URL share a cache dir but get different k83 resolver keys – the parallel-git race survives for that config. Refusing an empty ref in config (or normalising "" to absent everywhere) closes both this and the check issue above.

2026-09-26 17:03 Worker: source keys are exactly git/ref/url/local (SOURCE_KEYS); per-source vars/path do not exist, top-level vars already errors via asObject. url already errors on a non-string. Plan: git/ref/local present and not a string -> ConfigError '<file>: sources.<name>.<key> <json> must be a string'; ref "" refused ('must not be empty', hint to omit ref) rather than normalised – spec/README give "" no meaning, and add never writes an empty ref (pickDef/spec drop it). Tests first in test/config.test.ts.

